      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some warmth and redness can occur with a fresh muscle strain, new swelling that is visibly red and warm warrants medical attention to rule out a deep vein thrombosis (DVT). You should stop using your leg, elevate it immediately, and contact a healthcare provider or visit an urgent care clinic today rather than relying on ice alone. Only should you seek professional diagnosis, and follow their treatment plan strictly rather than waiting it out yourself.",
